# Button and control spacing

**Never place adjacent buttons or switches with no spacing.**

## Preferred: control cluster gap

```vue
<div class="d-flex align-center flex-wrap" style="gap: 8px">
  <v-btn variant="text">Cancel</v-btn>
  <v-btn color="primary" variant="elevated">Save</v-btn>
</div>
```

## Also OK: margin on the first of a fixed pair

```vue
<v-btn variant="text" class="mr-2" @click="cancel">Cancel</v-btn>
<v-btn color="primary" variant="elevated" @click="save">Save</v-btn>
```

Use `gap: 8px` for buttons, chips, and wrap toolbars. Do not use Vuetify `ga-*` utilities.

**Switch rows are different**: they use the `switch-cluster` theme class (16px), because an
inset switch's hit area already extends past its track and 8px reads as touching. See
`margins-and-spacing.mdc`.
